{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1873, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThere are N dice.\r\nThe i-th die has K_i faces, with the numbers A_{i,1}, A_{i,2}, \\ldots, A_{i,K_i} written on them.\r\nWhen you roll this die, each face appears with probability \\frac{1}{K_i}.\nYou choose two dice from the N dice and roll them.\r\nDetermine the maximum probability that the two dice show the same number, when the dice are chosen optimally.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nK_1 A_{1,1} A_{1,2} \\dots A_{1,K_1}\r\n\\vdots\r\nK_N A_{N,1} A_{N,2} \\dots A_{N,K_N}\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\r\nYour answer is considered correct if the absolute or relative error from the true solution does not exceed 10^{-8}.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2 \\leq N \\leq 100\n- 1 \\leq K_i\n- K_1 + K_2 + \\dots + K_N \\leq 10^5\n- 1 \\leq A_{i,j} \\leq 10^5\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3\r\n3 1 2 3\r\n4 1 2 2 1\r\n6 1 2 3 4 5 6\n\nSample Output 1\n\n0.333333333333333\r\n\n\n- When choosing the 1st and 2nd dice, the probability that the outcomes are the same is \\frac{1}{3}.\n- When choosing the 1st and 3rd dice, the probability is \\frac{1}{6}.\n- When choosing the 2nd and 3rd dice, the probability is \\frac{1}{6}.\n\nTherefore, the maximum probability is \\frac{1}{3} = 0.3333333333\\ldots.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3\r\n5 1 1 1 1 1\r\n4 2 2 2 2\r\n3 1 1 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0.666666666666667\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1951, "char_start": 1885, "quote": "Input:\n3\n3 1 2 3\n4 1 2 2 1\n6 1 2 3 4 5 6\nOutput:\n0.333333333333333", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2027, "char_start": 1963, "quote": "Input:\n3\n5 1 1 1 1 1\n4 2 2 2 2\n3 1 1 2\nOutput:\n0.666666666666667", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "ee5ced3feea6bc56351848e285d53e36e87a03c8aac5c71b59beacba4fe04683", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "551f805d856f4f77829283e7cad81905b6d57974982d2d271ba575a7f2c88652", "seq": 2}
